; GLCompatNull -- GLCompat through the RadeonGL minigl.library on the null
; card (uaegfx in FS-UAE, 2026-11-12), for GL 1.3 phase 1's Tex13Cases and
; everything before them. A bitmap context reaches the null card only when
; asked (SetEnv RadeonGLCard n; without it the library refuses, so a program
; learns nothing would be drawn). Nothing is drawn there, so the pixel
; checks FAIL by design; what it checks is the 68k build: every packet
; passes the library's checker ("checker errors: 0"), and the program ends.
; The pictures: gmake test (test_tex13) on the Mac, GLCompat on the card.
; Needs: gmake glsmoke.
; LIMIT 300
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Avail >NIL: FLUSH
Assign LIBS: DEV:GLSmoke/Libs ADD
SetEnv RadeonGLCard n
SetEnv RadeonGLLog DEV:Test/glcompat.log
Echo "=== GLCompat DEPTH=32 NOLOOP ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
DEV:GLSmoke/GLCompat DEPTH=32 NOLOOP >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "rc=$RC" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Assign LIBS: DEV:GLSmoke/Libs REMOVE
UnSetEnv RadeonGLCard
UnSetEnv RadeonGLLog
Echo "=== the library's log ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/glcompat.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
